  "literature_notes": "L9 (GFP-tagged M23-AQP4) names no loop, terminus, or residue for the tag position and therefore cannot be pinned to any site; it was not promoted. AQP4 has no extracellular N-terminus (the N-terminus, residues 1\u201336, is intracellular) and no signal peptide, so no terminal_n site is possible. The C-terminus (residues 253\u2013323) is also intracellular, ruling out a terminal_c surface site. ECL1 (58\u201369, 12 aa) and ECL2 (137\u2013155, 19 aa) are not mentioned in any ledger line as sites of insertion and were not proposed. Both qualifying sites map to the same loop (ECL3, 206\u2013231) but are grounded in separate papers with separate tag modalities (Myc vs. mRuby3), so they are reported as two distinct sites per the instructions.",
